{"game": "escape-from-duckov", "language": "english", "appid": 3167020, "month": "2026-02", "window": 1, "start_date": 1769904000, "end_date": 1770508799, "month_true_total": 375, "quota": 12, "returned": 12, "pulled_at": "2026-09-26 01:37:46 UTC", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "217813363", "author": {"steamid": "76561198068351377", "personaname": "yung moist", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/yung-moist/", "num_games_owned": 571, "num_reviews": 20, "playtime_forever": 2487, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 2487, "last_played": 1761979617, "avatar": "886f7b9c036d428aa94af73608bd3d5e7502d797"}, "language": "english", "review": "I'm only posting this review because a lot of people do not know how to read, which is par for the course due to declining literacy rates.\nMost of the mixed reviews involve controversy about a specific mod (SCAV Mode)\nWhat most people fail to mention consistently is that the devolopers actually endorsed the creators of the malicious mod and gave accolades to the creators of the mod even after they discovered malware, which is the main reason why it was review bombed.\n\nIf you're feeling unemployed, consult this thread for more details about the mod in question: https://steamcommunity.com/app/3167020/discussions/0/686366516152631949/\n\n\nAs for the game itself, it's a top down Tarkov that is a lot more forgiving in terms of difficulty. The gameplay loop involves collecting loot and blueprints to make yourself stronger while also upgrading your base with the loot you collect. The open world is large and compact with minimal empty space, and the bosses spread around the maps make the game more interesting due to how unique each enemy is. Ignoring the malicious mod itself, the game itself is worth it even at full price.", "timestamp_created": 1770502387, "timestamp_updated": 1770502387, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 4, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.505764365196228027